dhow | Spars hung | Each lateen mast gets one long yard, slung slantwise across it; the sail is laced along the yard. Also added: parrels and lateen sheet.

carrack | Yards crossed | The square-rigged masts cross four yards; the square sails hang from them. Braces at the yardarms swing the yards round to trim the sails to the wind. The lateen mast gets one long yard, slung slantwise across it; the sail is laced along the yard. The running rigging is rove: halyards, sheets, tacks and two more kinds of line. Also added: parrels, outlicker and lateen sheet.

fluyt | Yards crossed | The square-rigged masts cross six yards; the square sails hang from them. Braces at the yardarms swing the yards round to trim the sails to the wind. The lateen mast gets one long yard, slung slantwise across it; the sail is laced along the yard. The running rigging is rove: halyards, sheets, tacks and two more kinds of line. Also added: parrels, outlicker and lateen sheet.

east-indiaman | Yards crossed | The square-rigged masts cross nine yards; the square sails hang from them. Braces at the yardarms swing the yards round to trim the sails to the wind. The mizzen also gets a lateen yard, slung slantwise under its topsail; the lateen sail is laced along it. The running rigging is rove: halyards, sheets, tacks and two more kinds of line. Also added: parrels, outlicker and lateen sheet.

slave-ship | Yards crossed | The square-rigged masts cross nine yards; the square sails hang from them. Braces at the yardarms swing the yards round to trim the sails to the wind. The mizzen also gets a lateen yard, slung slantwise under its topsail; the lateen sail is laced along it. The running rigging is rove: halyards, sheets, tacks and two more kinds of line. Also added: parrels, outlicker and lateen sheet.

